{"company":{"id":"linkedin","name":"LinkedIn","accent":"#0a66c2","asset":"posts","verb":"open the feed"},"nodes":[{"id":"client","title":"App","kind":"client","blurb":"Feed, post, like, profile.","depth":0,"story":"This is the LinkedIn app on your phone or laptop. Tapping open the feed starts here. The app does not hold the whole product — it only starts the request."},{"id":"cdn","title":"CDN","kind":"cdn","blurb":"Images and video near the user.","depth":1,"story":"On LinkedIn, bulky posts are copied around the world. Play/browse should hit a nearby copy. If that copy is missing, a miss goes back to origin."},{"id":"api","title":"API gateway","kind":"api","blurb":"Write path and feed reads.","depth":1,"story":"Think of this as LinkedIn’s front desk. The app asks it for “what’s allowed / what’s next,” not for huge posts. It routes, limits traffic, and hides internal stores."},{"id":"auth","title":"Identity","kind":"auth","blurb":"Session and graph permissions.","depth":2,"story":"Before LinkedIn shows anything private, it checks who you are (account, session, device). A CDN copy of a file is not the same as being logged in."},{"id":"feed","title":"Feed service","kind":"service","blurb":"Assembles the ranked timeline.","depth":2,"story":"Your timeline is assembled and ranked. It is not “dump every post in the world in time order.”"},{"id":"post","title":"Post service","kind":"service","blurb":"Creates a post and kicks fan-out.","depth":2,"story":"Creating a post should feel instant. Telling millions of followers is leftover work on a queue."},{"id":"graph","title":"Social graph","kind":"service","blurb":"Followers / friends.","depth":3,"story":"Who follows whom. Fan-out and privacy both start from this graph."},{"id":"rank","title":"Ranker","kind":"service","blurb":"ML features → order of stories.","depth":3,"story":"Which story is on top. Signals (who you care about, what you watched) — not a random shuffle."},{"id":"cache","title":"Feed cache","kind":"cache","blurb":"Precomputed timelines for active users.","depth":3,"story":"The same questions get asked thousands of times (session, “is this still available?”). LinkedIn keeps those answers in fast memory so the main database is not hit every time."},{"id":"userdb","title":"User DB","kind":"db","blurb":"Profiles and settings.","depth":4,"story":"Your continue-watching / saved list lives here. It is tiny compared with posts, and it is queried often."},{"id":"postdb","title":"Post DB","kind":"db","blurb":"Captions, ids, pointers to media.","depth":4,"story":"This is LinkedIn’s notebook of records: accounts, titles, orders, messages. Small rows you can query — not the giant posts files."},{"id":"blob","title":"Media store","kind":"blob","blurb":"Original photos and videos.","depth":4,"story":"The warehouse for large posts. Cheap to store, not great for “show my last 20 items.” LinkedIn points at these files from the records database."},{"id":"queue","title":"Fan-out queue","kind":"queue","blurb":"Push ids to follower inboxes.","depth":5,"story":"Slow leftover work (encode, notify, payout) waits here after you already succeeded at open the feed. The tap can return; workers finish later."},{"id":"workers","title":"Fan-out workers","kind":"workers","blurb":"Write to many caches without blocking the poster.","depth":5,"story":"Background helpers at LinkedIn. They retry if something fails. They are not sitting on the button you just pressed."},{"id":"notify","title":"Notifications","kind":"workers","blurb":"Likes, comments, DMs.","depth":6,"story":"“New episode” or “your driver is here” is a background ping. It is not part of the Play / tap request that already succeeded."},{"id":"search","title":"Search / hashtags","kind":"service","blurb":"Secondary query path.","depth":6,"story":"Find inside files or posts. That is an index, not the warehouse itself."},{"id":"jobs-graph","title":"Jobs graph","kind":"service","blurb":"Connects skills, companies, recruiters, and candidates for ranking.","depth":6,"story":"Connects skills, companies, recruiters, and candidates for ranking."}],"edges":[{"from":"client","to":"cdn","label":"photos / video"},{"from":"client","to":"api","label":"feed / post"},{"from":"api","to":"auth","label":"who is this"},{"from":"api","to":"feed","label":"read timeline"},{"from":"api","to":"post","label":"create"},{"from":"feed","to":"rank","label":"order stories"},{"from":"feed","to":"cache","label":"precomputed feed"},{"from":"post","to":"graph","label":"followers"},{"from":"post","to":"queue","label":"fan-out job"},{"from":"queue","to":"workers","label":"write inboxes"},{"from":"workers","to":"cache","label":"update feeds"},{"from":"feed","to":"postdb","label":"post ids"},{"from":"graph","to":"userdb","label":"people"},{"from":"cdn","to":"blob","label":"media miss"},{"from":"post","to":"blob","label":"upload bytes"},{"from":"post","to":"notify","label":"ping followers"},{"from":"api","to":"search","label":"hashtags"},{"from":"workers","to":"jobs-graph","label":"update recommendations"}],"stages":[{"i":0,"blurb":"Pictures and video come from a nearby CDN. Likes, posts, and feed refresh go through an API.","unlockNodeIds":["client","cdn","api"],"unlockEdgeIds":["client->cdn","client->api","api->auth","api->feed","api->post","cdn->blob","api->search"]},{"i":1,"blurb":"Reading the feed and creating a post are two services. First, the system checks who you are.","unlockNodeIds":["auth","feed","post"],"unlockEdgeIds":["api->auth","api->feed","api->post","feed->rank","feed->cache","post->graph","post->queue","feed->postdb","post->blob","post->notify"]},{"i":2,"blurb":"Who you follow, a ranker, and a saved copy of the feed make scrolling feel instant.","unlockNodeIds":["graph","rank","cache"],"unlockEdgeIds":["feed->rank","feed->cache","post->graph","workers->cache","graph->userdb"]},{"i":3,"blurb":"People, post text, and photo files live in different stores on purpose.","unlockNodeIds":["userdb","postdb","blob"],"unlockEdgeIds":["feed->postdb","graph->userdb","cdn->blob","post->blob"]},{"i":4,"blurb":"Posting does not wait until every follower’s feed is updated. That work runs in the background.","unlockNodeIds":["queue","workers"],"unlockEdgeIds":["post->queue","queue->workers","workers->cache","workers->jobs-graph"]},{"i":5,"blurb":"Notifications and search are extra paths—not the same request as “create post.”","unlockNodeIds":["notify","search","jobs-graph"],"unlockEdgeIds":["post->notify","api->search"]}],"questions":[{"id":"linkedin-0-bytes-vs-control-0-0","stage":0,"tid":"bytes-vs-control","variant":0,"correct":"split-paths","distractors":["all-cdn","all-api","all-db"],"seed":3703118193},{"id":"linkedin-0-bytes-vs-control-0-1","stage":0,"tid":"bytes-vs-control","variant":1,"correct":"split-paths","distractors":["all-cdn","all-api","all-db"],"seed":3703118194},{"id":"linkedin-0-bytes-vs-control-0-2","stage":0,"tid":"bytes-vs-control","variant":2,"correct":"split-paths","distractors":["all-cdn","all-api","all-db"],"seed":3703118195},{"id":"linkedin-0-personalized-edge-0-0","stage":0,"tid":"personalized-edge","variant":0,"correct":"dont-cache-private","distractors":["cache-whole-home","one-origin","skip-edge"],"seed":1516351128},{"id":"linkedin-0-personalized-edge-0-1","stage":0,"tid":"personalized-edge","variant":1,"correct":"dont-cache-private","distractors":["cache-whole-home","one-origin","skip-edge"],"seed":1516351129},{"id":"linkedin-0-personalized-edge-0-2","stage":0,"tid":"personalized-edge","variant":2,"correct":"dont-cache-private","distractors":["cache-whole-home","one-origin","skip-edge"],"seed":1516351130},{"id":"linkedin-0-scene-friday-night-0-0","stage":0,"tid":"scene-friday-night","variant":0,"correct":"nearby-copy","distractors":["one-warehouse","through-db","wait-encode"],"seed":540130727},{"id":"linkedin-0-scene-wrong-path-0-0","stage":0,"tid":"scene-wrong-path","variant":0,"correct":"api-for-action","distractors":["cdn-for-save","db-from-phone","queue-for-play"],"seed":2